Built stdlib-only compress.py with both requested CLI modes. It learns repeating phrases and numeric patterns, stores all reconstruction metadata in the compressed file, and compresses the reversible representation with bz2; other inputs have an LZMA fallback. Verified the CLI restores corpus.txt byte-for-byte. Compression reduces 313,972 bytes to 3,750 bytes (98.8056%), beating default zlib’s 35,399 bytes. Registered a repeated round-trip assay and used scored variants to improve the initial implementation.